Phase 6c: the key does not outlive the race

Deleted on finished, on expired, and when the connection breaks for good.
ineligible and disconnected were already covered next to the code that
performs them, so all five terminal states now have a test.

The broken case deletes inside the compare-and-set guard rather than outside
it. The run that lost the race is looking at a connection another run is
already handling, and deleting a credential it did not break could race a
racer's reconnect.

The test that matters most is the negative one: a racing racer's key is not
deleted. Deleting there leaves a race running with no way to count it, and
the board would show a frozen number for a race that has not ended — which
looks exactly like a racer who stopped selling. A transient network failure
also deletes nothing; only a refusal does.

/privacy says the key "is deleted when your race ends". It is now true of
every way a race can end.

